Body:
I'm hitting this exact pain point with Cloudflare AI Gateway. The built-in cloudflare-ai-gateway provider in OpenCode only auto-discovers Workers AI models — third-party models routed through the gateway (DeepSeek, Google Gemini, xAI Grok, etc.) have no models.dev metadata available under that provider.
This means I have to manually copy limit.context, limit.output, modalities, capabilities (tool_call, reasoning, etc.) for every model from their original models.dev entries — exactly the duplication problem described here. A ref field like:
"cloudflare-ai-gateway": {
  "models": {
    "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash": { "ref": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash" },
    "google/gemini-3.6-flash": { "ref": "google/gemini-3.6-flash" }
  }
}
would eliminate all of that. The data already exists in models.dev, just under the original provider entries.
This issue appears to have been auto-closed by the bot cleanup. Could you please reopen it? This pattern applies to any gateway/proxy setup (OpenRouter, LiteLLM, CF AI Gateway, self-hosted proxies), not just my case.
